The contribution of intergranular γ′ precipitates on the damage accumulation of the powder
metallurgy superalloy N18 has been investigated. Electron microscopy investigations tend to link the
deformation of primary precipitates to γ particles forming within primary γ′ precipitates. Indeed,
these fine ductile particles can act as dislocation sources. The plasticity of primary precipitates
is, thus, assisted by the presence of γ particles and deformation incompatibilities are consequently
increased at γ/γ′ interfaces.

