2026-01-15 18:52:41,411 [INFO] root - [19] 来源: Modeling of the partitioning and phase transformation temperatures of an as-cast third generation single crystal Ni-base superalloy (块: None)
Cast single crystal Ni-base superalloys exhibit severe solidification segregation that must be
subsequently removed by solution heat treatment. In order to understand how some of the elements in
these alloys effect the solidification partitioning, the as-cast microstructure of the third
generation single crystal Ni-base superalloy, CMSX-10, was examined. In addition, the solidification
partitioning was calculated using Thermo-Calc™. The solidus, liquidus and γ′-solvus were also
calculated for the compositions of the base alloy, and determined compositions of the dendrite cores
and the interdendritic regions. All of the calculated values were compared to the experimentally
determined results of this study and areas for future work will be discussed.

2026-01-15 18:52:41,412 [INFO] root - [20] 来源: Microsegregation and homogenization behavior of a Ni-Co based refractory superalloy for turbine discs (块: None)
The as-cast microstructure and element segregation of a Ni-Co based alloy were investigated. The
effect of homogenization treatment on the microstructure and microsegregation was further discussed.
The results show that the precipitation phases in the as-cast microstructure of the Ni-Co based
alloy are γ' phase, primary MC carbide, eutectic γ/γ' phase and boride. The average secondary
dendrite arm in the as-cast alloy is about 39 μm. The Nb, Ti, Mo and Al are enriched in the
interdendrite region, while W, Co and Cr are opposite in the interdendrite region. The precipitates
were dissolved into the matric and segregation coefficient tend to close to one during
homogenization. Furthermore, the homogenization temperature of the Ni-Co based alloy can not exceed
1190 °C based on the results of isothermal quenching experiment. Diffusion of W in the Ni-Co based
alloy is the most sluggish during homogenization. The diffusion activation energy and diffusion
constant of W in the Ni-Co based alloy were calculated according to the residual segregation index
of W at different temperatures, which were 274.43 kJ/mol and 4.67 × 10−6 m2/s, respectively.
Finally, the homogenization kinetic of the Ni-Co based alloy was established in terms of a diffusion
model.

