2026-01-16 16:06:07,838 [INFO] root - [1] 来源: Effect of minor alloying additions on the carbide morphology in a single crystal Ni-base superalloy (块: None)
Carbon and boron have been added to single crystal Ni-base superalloys to increase the yield and
defect tolerance, but the effect of these additions on the solidification is not well understood.
Carbon was added to the second-generation single crystal Ni-base superalloy, CMSX-4, to form MC-type
carbides. Nitrogen and boron were also added in an attempt to alter the carbide morphology. This
investigation examines the effect of these alloying additions on the carbide morphology.

