2026-01-16 18:15:09,215 [INFO] root - [9] 来源: Phenomenon and Mechanism of High Temperature Low Plasticity in High-Cr Nickel-based Superalloy (块: None)
Cr is the most important element in nickel-based alloys to prevent high temperature oxidation and
corrosion. However, high-Cr content will lead to a decline of hot workability which limits the
addition of Cr for most nickel-based superalloys. In order to add more Cr into Ni-based alloy for
improving high temperature oxidation and corrosion resistance, the poor hot workability of high-Cr
alloy must be first solved. Deformation characteristic of a high-Cr nickel-based alloy (40 wt% Cr)
under hot compression conditions at 800−1200 °C has been investigated by using a Gleeble 3500
machine, and the microstructural evolution during hot working process has been observed by optical
microscopy and scanning electron microscopy. The results show that a high-temperature low-plasticity
(HTLP) region exists in this high-Cr nickel-based alloy. This phenomenon can be attributed to its
non-uniform interdendritic microstructure at high temperatures. These results can explain the poor
hot workability of high-Cr nickel-based alloy.

2026-01-16 18:15:09,216 [INFO] root - [10] 来源: Effect of rhenium addition on the microstructure of the superalloy Inconel 706 (块: None)
Alloying of single-crystal superalloys by Re (CMSX4, CMSX10, RR3000, etc.) decreases the coarsening
rate of γ′ precipitates. In order to clarify whether this effect works in the superalloy Inconel
706, its composition has been modified by adding about 2wt.% Re. Microstructure and composition of
the modified Inconel 706 superalloy are investigated by means of transmission electron microscopy
(TEM) and three-dimensional atom probe (3DAP) after long-term exposure at 750°C. 3DAP measurements
reveal the partitioning behavior of Re to the matrix in the 706 superalloy. It is found that the
stability of γ′ and γ″ precipitates is not significantly affected by the Re addition. The possible
reasons for this only weak Re effect on the superalloy Inconel 706 are discussed.

