2026-01-16 18:25:59,704 [INFO] root - [4] 来源: A novel Re-free Ni-based single-crystal superalloy with enhanced creep resistance and microstructure stability (块: None)
Rhenium (Re) is a paramount strengthening element in nickel-based single crystal superalloys because
of its low diffusion coefficient, high melting point and high partition coefficient between γ and γ'
phases. However, its detrimental influence on phase stability has remained a long-standing problem
to be solved. In this paper, we report a new design strategy to improve creep resistance and phase
stability of nickel-based single crystal superalloys by replacing Re by osmium (Os), which
contradicts the common belief. The experimental observations clearly show that the creep rate of
newly designed CSU-Os-2 alloy is lower than that of commercial CMSX-4 alloy at 980 °C/200 MPa/100 h.
Moreover, the CSU-Os-2 alloy also owns the better phase stability after exposure at 1100 °C for 1000
h, compared with CMSX-4 alloy. The striking properties can be well explained by higher partition
coefficient between γ and γ' phases and very likely lower diffusion coefficient of Os in γ matrix
than Re.

2026-01-16 18:25:59,708 [INFO] root - [5] 来源: The influence of the dendritic structure on the γ/γ′-lattice misfit in the single-crystal nickel-base superalloy CMSX-4 (块: None)
The γ/γ′-lattice misfit was measured locally by X-ray diffraction in the rhenium-containing single-
crystal nickel-base superalloy CMSX-4. Different sections of a single crystal casting and positions
in the dendritic structure have been analyzed. A remarkable difference of the misfit caused by
segregation of refractory elements was found between the dendrite center and periphery. Problems of
measurement and characterization of the γ/γ′-lattice misfit in superalloys of new generations with a
high refractory element level are discussed.

2026-01-16 18:25:59,708 [INFO] root - [6] 来源: Effect of rhenium addition on the microstructure of the superalloy Inconel 706 (块: None)
Alloying of single-crystal superalloys by Re (CMSX4, CMSX10, RR3000, etc.) decreases the coarsening
rate of γ′ precipitates. In order to clarify whether this effect works in the superalloy Inconel
706, its composition has been modified by adding about 2wt.% Re. Microstructure and composition of
the modified Inconel 706 superalloy are investigated by means of transmission electron microscopy
(TEM) and three-dimensional atom probe (3DAP) after long-term exposure at 750°C. 3DAP measurements
reveal the partitioning behavior of Re to the matrix in the 706 superalloy. It is found that the
stability of γ′ and γ″ precipitates is not significantly affected by the Re addition. The possible
reasons for this only weak Re effect on the superalloy Inconel 706 are discussed.

2026-01-16 18:25:59,709 [INFO] root - [7] 来源: Chemical composition measurements of a nickel-base superalloy by atom probe field ion microscopy (块: None)
Single crystals of the rhenium-containing nickel-base superalloy CMSX-4 were investigated using a
time of flight atom probe. The distribution of the alloying elements in the two phases, matrix (γ
phase) and precipitate (γ′ phase), was studied. The high spatial resolution of the atom probe allows
to analyse the γ−γ′ interface. The transition from matrix to γ′ phase takes place within one atomic
layer. The boundary is enriched with titanium. Layer-by-layer analysis of (001) planes of the L12
ordered γ′ phase reveals alternating Ni- and Al-rich planes. The probability of site occupation by
different elements could be evaluated. An approximate formula of the γ′ phase is given by (Ni81 Ti3
Ta2 Cr5 Co7 W2)3 (Ni20 Al70 Ta6 Co2 W2). Rhenium is found mainly in the matrix and has a tendency to
build clusters.

