A new, ordered L21 Heusler phase based on Ru2AlTa was identified in a heat-treated multicomponent
Ni-base superalloy containing high ruthenium. Such a phase has not previously been observed in
muticomponent Ni-base superalloys or in quaternary Ni–Al–Ta–Ru systems. The influence of
solidification-induced microsegregation on the formation and distribution of the Heusler phase is
discussed.

