2026-01-16 18:34:49,710 [INFO] root - [7] 来源: High temperature low cycle fatigue behaviour of UDIMET 720 Li superalloy (块: None)
The low cycle fatigue behaviour of UDIMET 720 Li has been investigated at 700 °C in vacuum and air
environments under strain control tests. Hold times (HTs) have been introduced at peak tensile
strain in order to determine the effects of creep and fatigue interactions. The fatigue life of the
alloy is practically independent of HT in both environments at high strain ranges while HT has
beneficial effect at low strain ranges. The main factor that adversely affects the life of the alloy
is oxidation, as the fatigue life is reduced in air compared to vacuum especially at high strain
ranges. The increase in fatigue due to HT at lower strain ranges is attributed to stress relaxation.
A life prediction model has shown that nucleation occurs after few cycles at high strain ranges
whereas a large proportion of the fatigue life is consumed in the nucleation process at low strain
ranges.

