2026-01-16 19:09:49,869 [INFO] root - [12] 来源: Stacking fault effects on dynamic strain aging in a Ni–Co-based superalloy (块: None)
In this work, statistical analyses are conducted to measure the stacking fault density and stacking
fault energy in a Ni–Co-based superalloy at different deformation temperatures and strain rates.
High stacking fault density and low stacking fault energy indicate that the dynamic strain aging
effects are caused by Suzuki segregation, which is enhanced by serious intersections of stacking
faults in the superalloy. These results provide new insight into understanding stacking fault
effects on dynamic strain aging in engineering alloys.

