2026-01-16 19:09:49,870 [INFO] root - [14] 来源: Lower temperature deformation mechanisms in a γ″-strengthened Ni-base superalloy (块: None)
Experimental observation of dislocation substructures after low temperature deformation in a
γ″-strengthened Ni-base alloy indicates that shearing by classical 1/2<110> dislocations producing
antiphase boundary formation in the γ″ phase may not be operative. Additionally, stacking faults are
not observed in the sheared matrix, so Shockley partial motion is not the sole operative mechanism.
These results have motivated the investigation of more complex deformation mechanisms through phase
field modeling of deformation modes in γ″. A novel set of γ″ variant dependent shearing modes are
presented.

