A more accurate life prediction for gas turbine blade takes into account the material behaviour
under the Low Cycle Fatigue cycles normally encountered in turbine operation. In this study, low
cycle fatigue tests are performed as the variables of total strain range and temperatures. The
relations between plastic and total strain energy densities and number of cycles to failure are
examined in order to predict the low cycle fatigue life of superalloy at different temperatures. The
fatigue lives that are predicted by Coffin-Manson method and strain energy methods are compared with
the measured fatigue lives at different temperatures.

