The influence of Ru on the creep behaviour of a Re-containing Ni-based single crystal alloy at high
temperature is investigated by creep capabilities measurement and microstructure evaluation. The
creep life of the Re alloy at 1100 C/137 MPa obtained is 164 h, after added 3.0%Ru, the creep
lifetime of 4.5Re/3Ru alloy at the same conditions is 321 h. The deforming characteristic of the
alloys during creep is dislocations gliding on  matrix and climbing over   phase. And a few
dislocations of shearing   phase may cross-glide for forming Kear-Wilsdorf (KW) locks in Re-
containing alloy. While more KW locks reserve in the   phase of 4.5Re/3Ru alloy. The reason of
4.5Re/3Ru alloy displaying an outstanding properties is put down to more Re, W atoms being
distributed in the  /  interface to delay dislocations shearing   phase and depress the sliding and
cross-sliding of dislocations. Wherein, the atoms Ru may replace the Al atoms in   phase, the
stronger bonding force between Ru atoms and Re, W, Mo promotes much more ones dissolving into
phase to delay the diffusion of them, this is deem as an important reason of the Re/Ru alloy
displaying an outstanding creep resistance at high temperature.

