A three-dimensional (3D) anisotropic finite element (FE) analysis was employed to analyse the
features about the elastic strain energy density, von Mises stress and hydrostatic pressure
distributions in Ni-based superalloy single crystals when external loads applied along the
[110]-direction. The asymmetry of the strain energy density, the von Mises stress and hydrostatic
pressure could be used to predict the raft morphology for alloys exhibiting a positive or negative
misfit. The reason was briefly discussed.

