2026-01-16 21:48:24,405 [INFO] root - [18] 来源: Creep deformation of a nickel-based single crystal superalloy under high stress at 1033 K (块: None)
The microstructure of a nickel-based single crystal superalloy has been investigated after creep
deformation at 1033 K under stress up to 850 MPa. High density of stacking faults are formed in γ′
precipitates during the creep deformation. At 700 MPa and 850 MPa, bi-directional stacking faults
are observed. These stacking faults are induced by the movement of a/3<112> partial dislocations.
Two formation mechanisms of a/3<112> partial dislocations, reaction and dissociation mechanisms, are
simultaneously observed in this alloy after deformation. The proportion of a/3<112> dislocations
formed by the dissociation mechanism increases as the applied stress increases. The primary creep
strain of this alloy is 2.45% at 850 MPa, which may be attributed to the combination of these two
mechanisms.

2026-01-16 21:48:24,405 [INFO] root - [19] 来源: In-situ observation of hydrogen induced crack initiation in a nickel-based superalloy (块: None)
Hydrogen induced crack initiation in a nickel-based superalloy was studied via in-situ Scanning
Electron Microscopy observation under slow strain rate loading. Direct evidence has been obtained of
crack initiation and propagation along dislocation slip bands leading to sample fracture. Post-
mortem microstructural analysis showed that hydrogen induced cracking and separation along
dislocation slip bands, which are along {111}γ crystallographic planes with the highest Schmid
factor, leads to the formation of the typical slip-trace-like features on the quasi-cleavage
surface.

