Topologically close-packed (TCP) phases seriously endanger the properties of Superalloy.
Investigating the microstructure of the TCP phases will provide a crystallographic reference for the
design of superalloys with better properties. The  phase is a common TCP phase in superalloys. It
belongs to the space group R-3 μm, and has a hexagonal structure with five Wyckoff sites of 3a, 18h,
