Creep data of Ni-based 19Cr-18Fe-3Mo-5Nb-Ti-Al superalloy (JIS NCF718-B) were obtained at 550C to
750C under 100MPa to 1000MPa and analyzed to determine the 100,000?h creep rupture strength. The
tensile properties were also evaluated at room temperature to 750C. Four heats of JIS NCF718-B were
used in this study. There was no large difference in the 0.2% proof stress and tensile strength
among the heats. A difference in the tensile ductility was observed at 650C to 750C among the heats.
Heat-to-heat variation of the creep rupture strength was confirmed among the heats and the variation
became large in the long term. Regression analysis was conducted for the tensile test data of the
four heats. The creep rupture data of all the heats were fitted to the regression equation of
logarithmic stress using the time C temperature parameters of Larson C Miller, Orr C Sherby C Dorn,
and Manson C Haferd to estimate the 100,000?h creep rupture strength. The Orr C Sherby C Dorn
parameter and regression equation of the second degree was suitable for the creep strength
evaluation.

