Creep properties at three different temperatures (1123, 1253 and 1373 K) for five single crystal
alloys with varying Re and W content are presented. Tungsten content has been varied between 3.0 and
3.6 wt.%, rhenium between 2.3 and 2.9 wt.%. Creep properties, such as minimum creep rate, time to
reach 1, or 2% strain and time to failure have been evaluated. For the low temperature regime, two
parts of rhenium can be replaced by one part of tungsten. In the intermediate range, the ratio
