microhardness of alloy decreased with an increase in temperature mainly due to the growth of γ′
phases. Elevated-temperature microhardness of alloy for standard heat-treated condition was higher
than room temperature microhardness. In comparison to NIMONIC alloy 263, the new alloy exhibited
higher ductility and higher tensile strength.

