2026-01-16 23:16:00,780 [INFO] root - [1] 来源: Effect of carbon content on microstructures and creep properties of a new Ni-Co-W based superalloy for turbine disc (块: None)
The grain boundary strength of wrought superalloys diminishes significantly with increasing
temperatures. Adjusting the carbon (C) content can enhance the carbides at grain boundaries, thereby
improving the creep properties of these alloys. The effect of C content on the microstructure and
creep properties of a novel Ni-Co-W based superalloy was investigated using thermodynamic
calculations, scanning electron microscopy (SEM), electron probe microanalysis (EPMA), and
transmission electron microscopy (TEM). The results indicate that both the quantity and size of MC
carbides increase with higher C content, and numerous small M23C6 carbide precipitates form at grain
boundaries. During creep at 800 °C/500 MPa, the increased C content strengthens the grain
boundaries, promotes grain boundary serration, hinders the formation of grain boundary cracks,
alters the fracture behavior of the alloy, and effectively enhances its creep life. Additionally,
during creep, increased grain boundary strength allows more dislocations to be transferred at grain
boundaries, resulting in more stacking faults and microtwins forming at service temperature. These
stacking faults and microtwins hinder further dislocation movement, thereby achieving synergistic
strengthening of both the grain boundaries and the intragranular regions. As the temperature further
increases to 850 °C, the grain boundary strength diminishes, and the efficiency of C in
strengthening the grain boundaries decreases accordingly. Nonetheless, C can still effectively
strengthen the grain boundaries of the alloy and inhibit the formation of grain boundary cracks
during creep.

