2026-01-16 23:48:37,985 [INFO] root - [6] 来源: Mechanical properties of Ni-based single-crystal Superalloy at 4.2 K (块: None)
This study investigates the extremely low temperature mechanical properties of Ni-based single-
crystal superalloy. Reduced yield strength and ductility occur at 4.2 K, owing to limited
dislocation mobility, γ′ precipitate interactions, and Kear-Wilsdorf locking. In addition, serrated
tensile behavior emerges at 4.2 K, yet amplitude remains limited at about 3 MPa.

