2026-01-17 00:45:55,036 [INFO] root - [12] 来源: Numerical simulation and experimental study of vacuum arc remelting (VAR) process for large-size GH4742 superalloy (块: None)
Numerical modeling and industrial experiment were used to study the entire vacuum arc remelting
(VAR) process of 660μmm GH4742 superalloy. In order to calculate the electromagnetic field, flow
field, temperature field, and melt pool shape change throughout the entire VAR process, a 2D
axisymmetric model with coupled multi-physical fields matching industry trials was constructed. The
microstructure and elemental distribution conditions in the large-size GH4742 ingot were analyzed in
combination with the industrial ingot dissection experiment, and the most likely locations of
freckle defects were predicted. According to the research, the melt pool has two clockwise flow
fields that are affected by buoyancy and Lorentz forces. The melt pool depth deepens gradually as
melting proceeds, with a maximum melt pool depth of 0.32μm and a paste zone width of 0.16μm.
Although the ingot's elemental distribution is largely consistent, there is microsegregation between
the dendrites. Where the freckle is most likely to appear, at (0.322, 0.075), the Rayleigh has a
great value of 1.1. For melt pool form and dendritic spacing throughout the entire melting process,
the results of the industrial ingot dissection experiment and the simulation results show good
agreement, proving the accuracy of the thermal history and solidification microstructure calculation
for the entire melting process. Furthermore, the prospect of combining numerical simulation with a
special material database for accurate defect prediction is proposed.

2026-01-17 00:45:55,037 [INFO] root - [13] 来源: The cracking behavior of the new Ni-based superalloy GH4151 in the triple melting process (块: None)
In this paper, the mechanism of crack formation in VIM, ESR, and VAR of GH4151 alloy ingots is
discussed. The cracks in VIM ingots are hot tearing, mainly caused by severe segregation of elements
such as Nb, Ti, and Al in VIM electrodes, which promotes the precipitation of (+α) eutectic and
Laves phases and thus leads to the formation of hot tearing. On the other hand, cracks in ESR and
VAR ingots are cold cracks caused by the uneven distribution of α phases. The temperature range for
the precipitation of (+α) eutectic phases is 1160CC1148°C, while that for α phases is 1137CC1072°C.
At temperatures below 884°C, the uneven precipitation of α phases results in a maximum internal
stress of 1096?MPa at room temperature. Based on computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations, to
avoid large internal stresses caused by the precipitation of α phase, the ingot should be removed
from the water-cooled crystallizer within 57μmin. Annealing is an effective measure to improve the
quality of electrodes. After annealing treatment, the α phase in the alloy transforms from short
rod-shaped to square-shaped, and the decomposition of Laves phase promotes the precipitation of
phase and  phase from the matrix, improving the mechanical properties of the alloy.

