2026-01-17 01:35:10,909 [INFO] root - [11] 来源: Preparation and isothermal oxidation resistance of Zr-doped PtAl coating on a Ni-based single crystal superalloy (块: None)
Two PtAl coatings with or without Zr-doped were prepared by electroplating Pt, vacuum diffusion
annealing, electroplating Ni or Ni-Zr layer, arc ion plating (AIP) and subsequently vacuum diffusion
annealing. The isothermal oxidation behavior of two coatings was investigated at 1100 ℃ for 500 h.
The spallation amounts of PtAl coating and Zr-doped PtAl coating are 0.031 mg/cm2 and 0.015 mg/cm2,
respectively. The results show that Zr-doped PtAl coating exhibited the excellent oxidation
resistance because Zr enhanced the compactness of oxide scale and slowed the transformation of β to
γ′ phase. In addition, the oxidation mechanism and effect of Zr on the anti-spallation resistance
and morphology of oxide scale was discussed.

2026-01-17 01:35:10,909 [INFO] root - [12] 来源: Sol–gel derived alumina layers on nickel-base superalloy Inconel-718 (IN-718) (块: None)
Modified Yoldas sols can be used to prepare crack-free well adherent layers on different substrate
materials such as soda–lime glass, corundum and metal (IN-718). These layers having thicknesses of
0.6 µm are strain tolerant and withstand thermal cycling between 810 °C and room temperature.
Introducing alpha-Al2O3 filler particles into modified Yoldas sols allows the preparation of thicker
layers of 1.6 µm, which as well can be thermally cycled without noticeable delaminations. Chemical
bonding seems to be the predominant layer bonding mechanism.

