The investigation of microstructure and properties of Ni-base alloy has been carried out after
various coating (one- and multi-layer) being deposited by EB PVD method and recovering heat
treatment being fulfilled. The optimal conditions of recovering heat treatment make it possible to
retain the entire complex of mechanical properties at the level typical for the alloy without
coating. The tests for cyclic strength of the blades with coatings have shown the advantage of
coatings with an external ceramic layer in comparison with metal coatings.

