This paper presents the phase stability and elemental partitioning in a
Co-40Ni-10Al-7.5W-10Cr-3Nb-0.06B-0.6C (at.%) superalloy (referred to as 3Nb) after a two-step heat
treatment. The resulting microstructure consisted of γ, γ′, MC carbides and µ-Co7W6 phase decorating
