tensile testing were conducted on as-HIPped samples. It was found that the fine powders promote the
formation of prior particle boundaries (PPBs) decorated with carbide and oxy-carbide clusters due to
the higher oxygen content per weight in fine powders, which adversely affects the mechanical
properties. It was also found that coarse powder particles are beneficial for minimising PPBs and
increasing the twin boundaries fraction. Nonetheless, the best balance of high temperature tensile
