2026-01-17 02:21:49,293 [INFO] root - [1] 来源: The interdendritic-melt solidification control (IMSC) and its effects on the porosity and phase change of a Ni-based superalloy (块: None)
A novel interdendritic-melt solidification control (IMSC) technique is developed to manufacture
equiaxed Ni-based superalloy with much reduced porosity. The basic concept of IMSC is illustrated.
The effects of IMSC on the porosity and phases of IN792 alloy are investigated using quantitative
metallography and synchrotron X-ray diffraction. Compared to conventional investment casting, IMSC
can produce castings with no shrinkage porosity, much less microporosity and larger dendritic arm
spacing, slightly larger sized eutectic (γ+γ′) and MC carbides, and has no significant effects on
the relative amount of phases.

2026-01-17 02:21:49,293 [INFO] root - [2] 来源: The cracking behavior of the new Ni-based superalloy GH4151 in the triple melting process (块: None)
In this paper, the mechanism of crack formation in VIM, ESR, and VAR of GH4151 alloy ingots is
discussed. The cracks in VIM ingots are hot tearing, mainly caused by severe segregation of elements
such as Nb, Ti, and Al in VIM electrodes, which promotes the precipitation of (+α) eutectic and
Laves phases and thus leads to the formation of hot tearing. On the other hand, cracks in ESR and
VAR ingots are cold cracks caused by the uneven distribution of α phases. The temperature range for
the precipitation of (+α) eutectic phases is 1160CC1148°C, while that for α phases is 1137CC1072°C.
At temperatures below 884°C, the uneven precipitation of α phases results in a maximum internal
stress of 1096?MPa at room temperature. Based on computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations, to
avoid large internal stresses caused by the precipitation of α phase, the ingot should be removed
from the water-cooled crystallizer within 57μmin. Annealing is an effective measure to improve the
quality of electrodes. After annealing treatment, the α phase in the alloy transforms from short
rod-shaped to square-shaped, and the decomposition of Laves phase promotes the precipitation of
phase and  phase from the matrix, improving the mechanical properties of the alloy.

