By means of microstructure observation and XRD analysis, the influence of heat treatment on phases'
constitution of IN718G superalloy was investigated. The results show that microstructure of IN718G
alloy consists of γ matrix, particle-like γ′, disc-like γ″ phases and needle-like δ phases. As the
aging time prolongs, the Nb atoms dissolve into the lattice of γ′ phase to promote the γ′ phase
being transformed into γ″-Ni3Nb phase, and the coherence interfaces are kept between the phases. The
calculation of First-principles indicated that in the γ′-Ni3Al and γ″-Ni3Nb phases may be co-existed
in the γ matrix, the 15.625(at.%) is thought to be the critical concentration of doping Nb for
promoting the transition of γ′-Ni3Al → γ″-Ni3Nb. Wherein, the close parameters of two phases in the
Nb doping range of 15.625–18.75(at.%) are thought to be the essential condition of the phase
transition of γ′-Ni3Al → γ″-Ni3Nb under coherence. During heat treatment, the Nb atoms of dissolved
into γ″ phase may promote its growth, while the Nb atoms of dissolved into γ′ phase may promote the
transition of γ′-Ni3Al → γ″-Ni3Nb phases. And the decomposition of γ′-Ni3Al phase may occur with the
precipitation and growth of γ″-Ni3Nb phase, which is thought to be the main reason of increasing the
volume fraction of γ″-Ni3Nb and diminishing the one of γ′-Ni3Al phase in the alloy.

