2026-01-26 17:24:36,734 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 4 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'Chromium (Cr) does not conform to the general rule observed in Ni–Al–X ternary phase diagrams—where the γ′ phase field is typically parallel to either the Ni–X or Al–X axis—because its presence is directly associated with lattice mismatch between the γ and γ′ phases. This deviation suggests that Cr influences or responds to the structural incompatibility between these phases, unlike other ternary additions (e.g., Ti, Nb, Pt, Re) that maintain coherent phase field orientations. The strong consistency between Cr and lattice mismatch indicates a unique role for Cr in altering phase stability or compatibility in nickel-based superalloys [cite: chunk-4a6d7a88bca36d648b3a4660df20875a-e-6, chunk-4a6d7a88bca36d648b3a4660df20875a-e-7, chunk-4a6d7a88bca36d648b3a4660df20875a-r-7].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Chromium (Cr) does not conform to the general rule observed in Ni–Al–X ternary phase diagrams—where the γ’ phase field is typically parallel to either the Ni–X or Al–X axis—because Cr and Co are enriched in the γ matrix rather than partitioning into the γ’ phase. This enrichment behavior indicates that Cr stabilizes or is preferentially soluble in the γ (FCC austenitic) matrix, which alters its influence on phase diagram topology compared to elements like Ti, Nb, or Re that strongly favor γ’ formation. As a result, Cr’s thermodynamic preference for the γ phase disrupts the typical alignment of the γ’ phase field seen with other ternary additions [cite: chunk-07e3f97c39cc8f0cf2c65a5771118f6e-e-12, chunk-07e3f97c39cc8f0cf2c65a5771118f6e-e-13, chunk-07e3f97c39cc8f0cf2c65a5771118f6e-r-11].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Chromium (Cr) at 30wt% does not conform to the typical γ′ phase field alignment seen in Ni–Al–X ternary systems (which are usually parallel to Ni–X or Al–X axes) because it plays a distinct role in enabling γ′ phase formation or stability through unique thermodynamic or kinetic effects, rather than following conventional solubility or substitutional behavior. This deviation suggests Cr influences the phase equilibrium in a way that alters the expected geometric orientation of the γ′ phase field in the ternary diagram [cite: chunk-f5c75066e293e1cfc17ff5ac60e52598-e-6, chunk-f5c75066e293e1cfc17ff5ac60e52598-e-7, chunk-f5c75066e293e1cfc17ff5ac60e52598-r-8].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Chromium (Cr) does not conform to the typical γ’ phase field alignment seen in Ni–Al–X ternary systems because it can substitute for aluminum in the L1₂ crystal structure of Ni₃Al, leading to a transformation from Ni₃Al to Ni₃Cr under certain conditions. This compositional substitution alters the phase stability and shifts the γ’ phase field away from the usual parallelism with either the Ni–X or Al–X axis observed for elements like Ti, Nb, Pt, or Re [cite: chunk-19e6e04ef0418a043d2ef116244b0098-e-8, chunk-19e6e04ef0418a043d2ef116244b0098-e-9, chunk-19e6e04ef0418a043d2ef116244b0098-r-10].', 'score': 8}]
