Boron addition to a new polycrystalline nickel-based superalloy promotes the formation of a hitherto
unreported aluminoborate phase, in the scale produced by oxidation in air at 900°C for ~10,000h.
Atom probe tomography provides unambiguous confirmation of this. The ramifications of its formation
are discussed.

