compression tests using superalloy 718 at deformation temperatures from 850 to 1100 C, a 67% height
reduction, and strain rates of 1, 10, and 25 s<sup>?1</sup> were performed to investigate the flow
stress behavior, which excludes environmental effects during hot working by inverse analysis. The
effects of dynamic recrystallization and strain-induced dynamic precipitation on the flow stress
were also investigated. The dynamically precipitated  phases deformed at 1050 C and <i></i> phases
