superalloy containing a high amount of tantalum was subjected to strength tests. Neither
tension/compression asymmetry nor mechanical twinning was observed in the creep test. However, the
tensile yield strength was higher than the compressive one, and micro-mechanical twinning was
observed in the compressive yielded microstructure using high resolution transmission electron
microscopy.

