The full elastic constants of Ni-based superalloy René 88DT were measured for the first time using a
recently developed method that matches the computed surface acoustic wave (SAW) velocities from an
elastodynamic model with experimental velocities of SAWs that are generated and detected with a
femtosecond laser. The experimental measurements were performed on several grains of a
polycrystalline sample without the need of growing a single crystal. The computed Young's modulus
from the resultant elastic constants agrees with the literature values, lending confidence on our
measured elastic constants: C11=267.1, C12=170.5, and C44=107.6 (GPa).

