The deformation mechanisms under tensile loading in a 45vol.% γ′ polycrystalline nickel-base
superalloy have been studied using neutron diffraction at 20°C, 400°C, 500°C, 650°C and 750°C with
the results interpreted via (self-consistent) polycrystal deformation modelling. The data
demonstrate that such experiments are suited to detecting changes of the γ′ slip mode from {111} to
