With increasing turbine inlet temperatures in aero-engines, the demand for temperature-resistant
turbine blades has led to the widespread use of nickel-based single crystal superalloys. These
alloys, known for their exceptional performance in high-temperature and high-stress environments,
incorporate advanced cooling structures like lamilloy and double wall cooling to enhance temperature
