addition, abnormal fine grains were observed at the bottom of the 40 mm specimen and the top of the
20 mm specimen. Large size α-W phases could be observed in these regions and are suggested to be the
cause of the grain refinement. The hardness test results showed that the hardness of the specimen
decreased as the cast thickness increased. The 975 °C/235 MPa rupture test results showed that the
rupture property decreased in the 40 mm specimen, but that there was no significant alteration in
the 3–20 mm specimens. These results provide a guidance for turbine blades manufacturing made from
this high W cast polycrystalline superalloy.

