of the base material and covered the surface of an unscaled region. In contrast, there was no oxide
on the surface of a scaled region, but it was replaced by several tiny particles remaining locally
on the outer surface of the base material. SEM-EDX and TEM-EDX point analysis of these particles
indicated not only the existence of high amounts of hafnium, but also several particles such as
