using Bridgman method. The effect of section size on the microstructure of the thin-walled specimens
of DD6 single crystal superalloy was investigated. The results show that with the reduction of
section size, the primary dendrite arm spacing and the eutectic percent of the thin-walled specimen
as-cast first decrease and then increase, and the average size of γ' phase in the dendritic core of
