A directionally solidified sample of superalloy CMSX-4 was investigated to show the effect of
crystal orientation on the segregation distribution. The solute distribution of alloying elements
across a dendritic cell was measured. Due to the preferred crystal growth in <100> orientation the
segregation profiles in this direction is much flatter than that in <110> orientation.

