The orientational dependence of microstructure evolution and the relevant deformation mechanism of a
single crystal superalloy were investigated. It showed that the annealing microstructures of below
the γ’ solvus were strongly associated with the deformation distribution between the γ’ phase and
the matrix. Several influence factors concerning the anisotropic deformation distribution were
discussed in <001><011> and <111> orientations in this paper. It was concluded that orientations
