2026-01-26 18:53:36,387 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 5 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'The preferred growth direction of single crystal superalloys, such as the <001> orientation (often referred to as <100> in cubic systems), is critical because it maximizes mechanical performance—particularly resistance to creep and thermal fatigue—by aligning the crystal lattice along directions that minimize energy and enhance structural stability under high-stress, high-temperature conditions like those in turbine blades. This alignment is a foundational requirement, as the absence of grain boundaries in single crystals only delivers performance benefits when the lattice is precisely oriented [cite: chunk-c1e910ea338b545267414d8a5325e83f-e-1, chunk-c1e910ea338b545267414d8a5325e83f-e-2, chunk-c1e910ea338b545267414d8a5325e83f-r-1].', 'score': 10}, {'answer': 'The [001] crystallographic orientation (aligned with the <100> growth direction) is considered optimal for Ni-based single-crystal superalloys like SRR99 because it exhibits superior mechanical performance under high-temperature conditions, despite still being susceptible to short cracks. This orientation minimizes detrimental effects from micropores and offers better resistance to crack propagation compared to other orientations such as [011] and [111]. [cite: chunk-2a1a7efef913310514e28961f65fc97b-r-1, chunk-b9326c8a891c693872d79ec7b29611c0-r-9, chunk-23033c43fd11b16c51f050350cc593ec-r-7]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The context confirms that single-crystal DD5 superalloy is explicitly associated with the (001) crystallographic orientation, which aligns with the <100> family of directions in cubic crystals like nickel-based superalloys. This orientation is preferred because it enables optimal mechanical properties—such as high creep resistance—critical for high-temperature applications like turbine blades. The data indicates that only the single-crystal form (E4) definitively possesses this orientation due to controlled growth processes, unlike polycrystalline variants where such alignment is uncertain [cite: chunk-69740559bbed66ff9c064c5a83413c79-e-9, chunk-69740559bbed66ff9c064c5a83413c79-e-6, chunk-69740559bbed66ff9c064c5a83413c79-r-12].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The preferred growth direction of a single crystal superalloy is <100> because there exists a definitive angular relationship between [100] orientations and the thermal gradient direction, indicating that crystal alignment is structured relative to heat flow. This alignment influences thermal transport properties and microstructural evolution during thermal processing, which is critical in applications like directional solidification and additive manufacturing where controlling crystal orientation enhances material performance [cite: chunk-6a3909dbfd9629821de298ce61279024-e-13, chunk-6a3909dbfd9629821de298ce61279024-e-14, chunk-6a3909dbfd9629821de298ce61279024-r-11].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The preferred growth direction of the single crystal superalloy is [001], which aligns with the <100> crystallographic family, because specimens oriented in this direction are specifically used in high-temperature mechanical tests such as dwell-fatigue and variable strain rate tensile testing, indicating its mechanical and microstructural advantages under operational conditions. [cite: chunk-4201d696f296c7b1a8dfadcb948fe14a-e-6, chunk-2b291e8ecc964c0b9ef05731d776747d-e-1, chunk-2b291e8ecc964c0b9ef05731d776747d-r-1, chunk-2b291e8ecc964c0b9ef05731d776747d-r-2, chunk-2b291e8ecc964c0b9ef05731d776747d-r-3]', 'score': 9}]
