2026-01-26 19:20:42,525 [INFO] root - [4] 来源: Effect of carbon addition on the creep properties in a Ni-based single crystal superalloy (块: None)
Effect of minor carbon addition on the creep properties of an experimental Ni-based single crystal
superalloy has been investigated. Three alloys with different level of carbon addition were
subjected to creep tests of 871°C/552MPa and 1038°C/172MPa. With the increase of carbon addition,
the creep properties of alloys presented different trends. Detailed microstructural analysis have
revealed that precipitation of M6C carbide and reduction of casting pores are beneficial to the
creep properties, and the improvement at high temperature and low stress is stronger than that at
low temperature and high stress. The larger γ′ particle, eutectic and MC carbide are the weakening
factors for creep properties; however, the weakening effect at high temperature and low stress is
weaker than that at low temperature and high stress.

2026-01-26 19:20:42,525 [INFO] root - [5] 来源: Creep performance in a CoNi-based single crystal superalloy with super-high α volume fraction at 760°C and equivalent high stress (块: None)
The creep performance at low temperature and high stress is one crucial property for the single
crystal superalloys widely used for turbine blades. In this study, the creep behavior of a CoNi-
based single crystal superalloy with super-high α volume fraction (Vα?=?90%) was investigated at
760°C/550?MPa based on microstructural ( and α phases) and deformation substructural (dislocations,
anti-phase boundaries (APBs) and stacking faults (SFs)) analyses to reveal its creep mechanism under
low temperature/high stress conditions. The super-high Vα contributes to the rapid transformation of
creep mechanisms from the matrix dislocation movement in the initial decelerating stage to the APB-
coupled dislocation pairs and their evolving non-planar SF ribbons inside γ\' precipitates during
the accelerating stage. In the following second decelerating stage, the interactions between SFs and
APBs improve the deformation resistance of α precipitates and decrease the creep rate. Subsequently,
the high density of APBs is believed to play a significant role in microstructural stability and
promotes the accumulation of matrix dislocations, which is responsible for the steady and final
accelerating stages. Appropriate Vα and increasing the APB energy are assumed to improve the creep
resistance of CoNi-based single crystal superalloys by enhancing the strengthening effect of
dislocation accumulation in  matrix and critical shear stress of α phase.

2026-01-26 19:20:42,526 [INFO] root - [6] 来源: Effect of ruthenium on compressive creep of Ni-based single-crystal superalloy (块: None)
Effects of Ru on the compressive creep of Ni-based single-crystal superalloys were investigated at
750 and 900°C. The addition of Ru improved the creep strength at 750°C. It enhanced the dissociation
of dislocations in the matrix channels and would inhibit the nucleation of the a〈112〉 dislocation
ribbons which shear the matrix and the precipitates; as a result, the mechanical-twin formation was
also impeded and creep strength was increased. However, Ru addition did not improve creep strength
at 900°C.

