2026-01-26 19:47:29,630 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 9 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'The γ′ phase in nickel-base superalloys is often cuboidal because it forms as a coherent precipitate (Ni₃(Al,Ti)) within the γ matrix, and its cuboidal morphology minimizes interfacial energy while maintaining coherency with the surrounding matrix. This shape enhances resistance to dislocation motion at elevated temperatures, which is critical for high-temperature strength and creep resistance—especially in single-crystal configurations used in aerospace turbine blades [cite: chunk-e711ea9893c91fd5ce884c423d1ba069-e-1, chunk-e711ea9893c91fd5ce884c423d1ba069-e-2, chunk-e711ea9893c91fd5ce884c423d1ba069-r-1].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The gamma prime (γ’) phase in nickel-base superalloys is often cuboidal because the gamma/gamma prime microstructure exhibits a cube-cube orientation relationship, which aligns the crystallographic planes of the γ and γ’ phases along cubic symmetry directions. This alignment minimizes interfacial energy and promotes coherent or semi-coherent phase boundaries, stabilizing the cuboidal morphology [cite: chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-e-3, chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-e-2, chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-r-1].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': "The γ'-phase in nickel-based superalloys often adopts a cuboidal morphology to minimize interfacial energy at the coherent or semi-coherent boundary with the γ-phase matrix, which enhances mechanical strength by effectively impeding dislocation motion—especially under high-temperature conditions. This shape is energetically favorable due to the lattice mismatch and crystallographic alignment between the two phases [cite: chunk-e076e24ea359e7c9ff98aa173a1d1897-e-9, chunk-e076e24ea359e7c9ff98aa173a1d1897-e-10, chunk-e076e24ea359e7c9ff98aa173a1d1897-r-18].", 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The γ’ phase in nickel-base superalloys adopts a cuboidal morphology to minimize interfacial energy with the surrounding γ matrix due to its coherent L1₂ crystal structure and lattice mismatch, which promotes ordered precipitate growth along specific crystallographic directions. This shape enhances mechanical strength by impeding dislocation motion while maintaining coherency strain at the γ/γ’ interface [cite: chunk-5a7b9157cadfeedb765f8124d9fc180e-e-10, chunk-5a7b9157cadfeedb765f8124d9fc180e-e-11, chunk-5a7b9157cadfeedb765f8124d9fc180e-r-12].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'In the studied nickel-based superalloy (NNS), the γ′ phase adopts a cubic morphology specifically when subjected to heat treatment at 1175\u202f℃, indicating that high-temperature thermal processing drives the formation of cuboidal γ′ precipitates [cite: chunk-51c40a9c5b354438dcc99e3538fa77b3-e-5, chunk-51c40a9c5b354438dcc99e3538fa77b3-e-8, chunk-51c40a9c5b354438dcc99e3538fa77b3-r-7]. This cuboidal shape enhances mechanical strength by effectively hindering dislocation slip, which in turn reinforces the stability of the cubic γ′ structure itself [cite: chunk-51c40a9c5b354438dcc99e3538fa77b3-e-16, chunk-51c40a9c5b354438dcc99e3538fa77b3-e-8, chunk-51c40a9c5b354438dcc99e3538fa77b3-r-16]. Thus, the cuboidal form is not inherent but thermally induced and functionally advantageous for high-temperature performance.', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The γ′-precipitates in nickel-based superalloys form cuboidal shapes due to their coherent interface and lattice matching with the surrounding γ matrix, which minimizes interfacial energy during self-assembly. This morphology enhances mechanical properties by impeding dislocation motion, contributing to high-temperature strength and creep resistance [cite: chunk-1d0558dd6b356e0f049b56cabb437fd5-e-1, chunk-1d0558dd6b356e0f049b56cabb437fd5-e-2, chunk-1d0558dd6b356e0f049b56cabb437fd5-r-1].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'The γ′ phase in nickel-based superalloys often adopts a cuboidal morphology due to coherent or semi-coherent interfacial relationships with the matrix phase, which minimize interfacial energy. A perfect crystallographic match—such as between the (11̅0) plane of the β phase and the (11̅1) plane of the γ′ phase with a matching score of 1.0—promotes this coherency, stabilizing cube-like precipitates that enhance mechanical properties like strength and creep resistance at high temperatures [cite: chunk-a4879f76f4fd7e3b4b7e43d924b5fa81-e-6, chunk-a4879f76f4fd7e3b4b7e43d924b5fa81-e-7, chunk-a4879f76f4fd7e3b4b7e43d924b5fa81-r-5].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Coherency between the gamma matrix and gamma prime precipitates contributes to the cuboidal shape of the γ’ phase. High coherency, enabled by lattice matching at the interface, reduces interfacial defects and strain, which—combined with the cube-cube orientation relationship—favors the development of cuboidal precipitates that enhance mechanical properties like creep resistance [cite: chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-e-3, chunk-5d942c8f1c01db54bab51b31faea4836-e-7, chunk-5d942c8f1c01db54bab51b31faea4836-r-4].', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'The interdependence between the cube-cube orientation relationship and coherency indirectly supports the cuboidal morphology of the γ’ phase. By aligning crystallographic planes and minimizing interfacial energy, these features synergistically stabilize the cuboidal shape, which is critical for high-temperature strength in nickel-based superalloys [cite: chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-e-3, chunk-5d942c8f1c01db54bab51b31faea4836-e-7, chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-e-2, chunk-0e400a717c0177b6e54870a3d685e980-r-1, chunk-5d942c8f1c01db54bab51b31faea4836-r-4].', 'score': 7}]
