crystallographic cracking at low temperature. To clarify these behaviors, fatigue crack propagation
test at 450 °C and crystal plasticity analysis are conducted for a Ni-base single crystal
superalloy. The Mode I cracking, the transition, and the crystallographic cracking are observed to
be dependent on the level of stress intensity factor range, and to be affected by the
crystallographic orientations in a compact specimen. Crystal plasticity finite element analysis for
