crystallographic planes compared to Mode I, which is important to account for in crack growth life
predictions. In this paper, a method to evaluate the crystallographic fatigue crack growth rate,
based on a previously developed crystallographic crack driving force parameter, is presented. The
crystallographic crack growth rate was determined by evaluating heat tints on the fracture surfaces
