2026-01-26 20:14:56,763 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 3 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'During engine start-up, as the hollow turbine blade heats from the outside in, creep initiates near the hotter outer surfaces, which gradually reduces their load-carrying capacity. This shifts more mechanical load to the internal (cooler) webs of the blade, which remain stiffer and less prone to creep initially. The described testing framework supports this analysis: the simplified blade model (E1) is subjected to simultaneous thermal loading via a high-frequency induction coil (E8) and mechanical loading (E4), while strain and temperature are monitored using extensometers (E6) and thermocouples (E7). These measurements, combined with FE calculations (E3) and ABAQUS-FE simulations (E5), enable detailed modeling of thermo-mechanical stress redistribution during transient heating—directly relevant to understanding how creep in outer regions affects internal web loading [cite: chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-3, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-9, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-8, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-6, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-5, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-4, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-3, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-5, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-4, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-7, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-8].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': "During engine start-up, as the hollow turbine blade heats up from outside in, creep initiates first near the outer surfaces. This localized creep can redistribute mechanical loads toward the cooler internal webs, which remain stiffer and thus bear a greater share of the structural load. The context indicates that high-temperature rotating components experience concurrent Type I cyclic loading, Type III/IV cyclic loading, and creep loading, with moderate coexistence (score=0.5). Furthermore, Type III/IV cyclic loading both 'varies with' and 'has limited effect on' creep loading (scores=0.4), suggesting that as creep progresses in the outer regions, the cyclic loading experienced by internal structures may be modulated—potentially increasing stress concentrations in cooler zones that have not yet undergone creep relaxation. [cite: chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-e-1, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-e-2, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-e-3, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-e-4, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-r-1, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-r-2, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-r-3, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-r-4, chunk-95409a5d1d55869b243464e4889c75f7-r-9]", 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'As the hollow turbine blade heats up from the outside during engine start-up, creep initiates first in the outer surfaces due to higher temperatures. This time-dependent deformation alters the local stress fields, effectively redistributing mechanical load toward the cooler internal webs that have not yet undergone significant creep. Since creep mechanisms are known to explain elevated ΔK (stress intensity factor range) values, the resulting stress redistribution may increase the effective ΔK experienced by the internal webs, potentially accelerating crack growth or structural degradation in those regions [cite: chunk-4e9ae6ebb60d08dd140ea833014597d3-e-13, chunk-4e9ae6ebb60d08dd140ea833014597d3-e-15, chunk-4e9ae6ebb60d08dd140ea833014597d3-r-9].', 'score': 8}]
