2026-01-26 20:28:29,835 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 20 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'Turbine blade failure can occur due to tip cracks that both result from and exacerbate operational stresses, creating a feedback loop of degradation. [cite: chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-1, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-3, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-2, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-3]', 'score': 10}, {'answer': 'A K403 turbine blade might be considered failed due to mechanical property degradation (E3), which is strongly caused by microstructure degradation (E1) [cite: chunk-faa1691ea9e46858c26f64d488fe73b7-r-1, chunk-faa1691ea9e46858c26f64d488fe73b7-r-2].', 'score': 10}, {'answer': 'Low-cycle fatigue (LCF) can lead to crack initiation driven by stress concentration, high misorientation factors, and slip system activation, all of which accelerate microstructural damage and eventual macroscopic failure [cite: chunk-89d564ce28954cbb960fc223c6f28b17-e-2, chunk-ed84e701f59ede6b9d64fc542ae54ff7-e-7, chunk-1b8454618c088ae773c1cdbbb1bafcc4-e-15, chunk-451d620bec118eb564dc2ca3ba3b3a4c-e-7, chunk-422be4ddc4fa3a7dd7206da2f622dd6e-e-3, chunk-ed84e701f59ede6b9d64fc542ae54ff7-r-5, chunk-8f2a803e89ef07c67706886e91b1ec52-r-6, chunk-451d620bec118eb564dc2ca3ba3b3a4c-r-7, chunk-451d620bec118eb564dc2ca3ba3b3a4c-r-6, chunk-de89da5a1165595bddd7fd9387b0b9cf-r-4].', 'score': 10}, {'answer': "Turbine blades might be considered to have 'failed' due to cracking, erosion, or foreign object damage. These forms of degradation compromise blade integrity and can lead to uncontained engine failures, loss of thrust, or in-flight shutdowns, directly jeopardizing aeroengine safety [cite: chunk-c27d8b0655550f57dcafa36eef1492f7-e-1, chunk-c27d8b0655550f57dcafa36eef1492f7-e-2, chunk-c27d8b0655550f57dcafa36eef1492f7-r-1].", 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Blade tip cracks actively contribute to increased environmental and thermal stress, which can accelerate fatigue, oxidation, or creep—leading to functional failure even if the blade remains structurally intact. [cite: chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-3, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-5, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-5]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Despite protective measures like oxidation- and abrasion-resistant coatings on the squealer tip, the underlying nickel-based superalloy remains susceptible to degradation under high-temperature operational stresses, which can lead to material-level failure. [cite: chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-1, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-2, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-6, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-7, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-1, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-6, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-7]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Diffusion of heavy alloying elements like rhenium toward the surface can alter local chemistry and mechanical properties, potentially leading to phase instability or coating spallation—key failure modes in high-temperature turbine environments [cite: chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-4, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-8, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-3, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-9].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Turbine blades, particularly in hot sections of industrial gas turbines, may fail due to thermo-mechanical fatigue—a key degradation mechanism affecting both coatings and advanced superalloys used in these components [cite: chunk-556d820ddbae9c9c730e555ef87312a3-e-5, chunk-3ec65f62dedc4ea3989ce569a132d1c2-e-2, chunk-3ec65f62dedc4ea3989ce569a132d1c2-e-6, chunk-3ec65f62dedc4ea3989ce569a132d1c2-r-8, chunk-3ec65f62dedc4ea3989ce569a132d1c2-r-7].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Turbine blades may fail due to thermomechanical fatigue (TMF), which causes material failure despite sometimes exhibiting longer lifetimes than isothermal fatigue under specific conditions, particularly in in-phase loading scenarios that promote cyclic softening [cite: chunk-2f110c504f796ebae60b63ff44898e94-e-2, chunk-aeba365a4468be09497d074a9481aa51-e-4, chunk-1ef08f311617943578862e7ecb6b42a1-e-6, chunk-6d62b8d29c1974b0feca8efabffc4f2f-e-5, chunk-ed18d10eca6fe7ef5a50e4a6ef1c7b4a-e-3, chunk-dcabec43f1f2206a87597ccc217e55d1-e-6, chunk-c158eae90dbabc59e86b7f63c851315e-r-1, chunk-c2294b87040b536130f486ede79e80ed-r-1, chunk-2f110c504f796ebae60b63ff44898e94-r-5, chunk-2f110c504f796ebae60b63ff44898e94-r-3, chunk-75c5b504583ddab98d2cbfad2501a9ed-r-3].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Cyclic softening—a consistent response in nickel-based superalloys like FGH96 and FGH4098 under both LCF and TMF—can reduce load-bearing capacity over time, accelerating crack initiation and contributing to premature failure [cite: chunk-e7b6d3894758ab792a9c44750dea67e3-e-1, chunk-b1540b5840ad1740aadaa5b07895ee50-e-1, chunk-dcabec43f1f2206a87597ccc217e55d1-e-6, chunk-82946f3032b47cc2184f49123ca6e4c9-e-11, chunk-6aa72a0a4925579e07ba06d5194eb1f5-e-2, chunk-ed18d10eca6fe7ef5a50e4a6ef1c7b4a-e-3, chunk-85aa9d888e016455de323d725289bba8-r-1, chunk-ed18d10eca6fe7ef5a50e4a6ef1c7b4a-r-5, chunk-a6b0b1e8243b23de1925c8f97699a972-r-17, chunk-6e21ca72d95c5df757392d73e2be6f50-r-2, chunk-a5f7c290bbcdfd69ead779220d3303a7-r-7, chunk-75c5b504583ddab98d2cbfad2501a9ed-r-3].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Secondary damage mechanisms such as rubbing and corrosion further degrade the blade surface, compounding the effects of cracking and thermal stress and potentially leading to premature failure. [cite: chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-1, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-e-4, chunk-ca27abbb0a01727180386b2913f6ce86-r-4]', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'Single crystal turbine blades may fail due to material heterogeneities—specifically, both chemical (E2) and microstructural (E3) non-uniformities—which are exacerbated by the blades themselves. These heterogeneities can act as initiation sites for cracks or corrosion under high-temperature and high-stress conditions, ultimately reducing reliability and service life [cite: chunk-6949756d1864ae01060d9c0694e0c5c0-e-1, chunk-6949756d1864ae01060d9c0694e0c5c0-e-4, chunk-6949756d1864ae01060d9c0694e0c5c0-e-3, chunk-6949756d1864ae01060d9c0694e0c5c0-r-1, chunk-6949756d1864ae01060d9c0694e0c5c0-r-2].', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'Failure may also be inferred when the blade’s condition no longer supports reliable prediction of residual properties (E6), indicating it has degraded beyond usable operational thresholds [cite: chunk-faa1691ea9e46858c26f64d488fe73b7-r-6].', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'In the context of internally cooled turbine blades, failure modes include thermal fatigue and creep, which arise from extreme thermal environments and steady-state mechanical stress—conditions emulated in the testing framework using a high-frequency induction coil for heating and constant mechanical loading [cite: chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-3, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-9, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-8, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-6, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-e-5, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-3, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-5, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-4, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-7, chunk-a16773290bfa56b35bc2d9ae4b4ba22c-r-8]', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'Turbine blade failure may occur due to complex oxidation and diffusion processes that degrade material integrity. The surface scale on nickel-based single crystal turbine blades contains hafnium oxides, rhenium-rich particles, and tiny embedded particles, indicating non-uniform, multiphase oxidation that can compromise structural stability [cite: chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-1, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-2, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-3, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-4, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-6, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-1, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-2, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-3, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-5].', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'The protective aluminium oxide layer beneath the aerofoil is not pristine but contains embedded tiny particles that may act as defect sites or stress concentrators, reducing oxidation resistance and potentially initiating cracks or delamination [cite: chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-2, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-5, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-6, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-4, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-7].', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'While the context does not explicitly list all possible turbine blade failure modes, it highlights that blading imposes significant stress on vibrational or resonant dynamics, which can lead to failure. Specifically, cyclic loading from aerodynamic or fluid forces on blades may excite natural frequencies, causing resonance. Unmitigated resonance can accelerate fatigue, reduce operational lifespan, or trigger catastrophic failure [cite: chunk-cdded3befa5ee7c187ddd24acee4b703-e-7, chunk-cdded3befa5ee7c187ddd24acee4b703-e-6, chunk-cdded3befa5ee7c187ddd24acee4b703-r-4].', 'score': 7}, {'answer': 'Co-location of zirconium within hafnium oxides may influence scale adhesion and thermal barrier coating performance, suggesting potential failure through reduced coating durability or interfacial delamination under thermal cycling [cite: chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-3, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-7, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-e-6, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-6, chunk-313c8554d7b68d1a4650c4013f016c40-r-8].', 'score': 7}, {'answer': 'Secondary failure indicators could include anomalous spatial structural features (E4) or irregular carbon element behavior (E5), both of which correlate with microstructure degradation and may signal localized material instability [cite: chunk-faa1691ea9e46858c26f64d488fe73b7-r-3, chunk-faa1691ea9e46858c26f64d488fe73b7-r-4].', 'score': 6}, {'answer': 'While the provided context does not explicitly list all possible reasons for turbine-blade failure, it implies that degradation or failure of the Thermal Barrier Coating (TBC) system—used in turbines—can lead to turbine inefficiency, increased maintenance costs, or unplanned downtime. Since TBC protects turbine components from high-temperature degradation, its failure could result in thermal damage, reduced component lifespan, or operational inefficiencies, which may constitute practical modes of turbine-blade failure [cite: chunk-5abc3c05849dadfca952537bf1c8dc41-e-5, chunk-5abc3c05849dadfca952537bf1c8dc41-e-6, chunk-5abc3c05849dadfca952537bf1c8dc41-r-3].', 'score': 6}]
