melting progresses the simulated molten pool morphology changes from a "shallow flat" shape to a
"shallow U " shape. After melting for 500 minutes the depth of the molten pool and the width of the
mushy zone tend to stabilize with maximum molten pool depth and mushy zone width being 200.88 mm and
72.38 mm respectively. During stable melting the cooling rate at the surface and center of the
casting ingot is 0.126K / s and 0.009 K/s respectively and after the height of the ingot is exceeds
0.4 μm the cooling rate of the casting ingot is basically stable.The trajectories of six particle
size inclusions in the molten pool were simulated. Large size inclusions &gt;20 μm were subjected to
the fluid flow and buoyancy to move helically in the molten pool and were eventually trapped at the
ingot sidewalls while small size inclusions 10 μm entered the molten pool and then moved inward
along the bottom of the pool eventually remaining inside the ingot which is basically consistent
with the detection value of the industrial ingot.

