2026-01-26 21:31:40,189 [INFO] root - [2] 来源: Unexpected formation of delta (δ) phase in as-cast niobium-bearing superalloy at solution annealing temperatures (块: None)
The annealing of as-cast Inconel 718 superalloy at high solution annealing temperatures for short
holding durations was studied. It was found that the needle-shaped δ phase formed from the eutectic
constituent, which was followed by the dissolution of this phase by continued annealing. In fact,
the formation of δ phase was characterized as an intermediate stage for the dissolution of Laves
phase and back-diffusion of the segregated elements from the interdendritic regions. Thermodynamics
analysis revealed that the upper temperature limit for the formation of δ phase is dependent on the
Nb content. During annealing, the Laves phase started to dissolve, which resulted in the rejection
