Boron segregation and boride formation at grain boundaries are generally accepted in Ni-based
superalloys. However, the addition of boron was found to result in the formation of a high density
of nanosized M5B3 (where M is a mixture of Cr, Mo) particles in γ/γ′ eutectics of a Ni-based
