improving the creep properties of these alloys. The effect of C content on the microstructure and
creep properties of a novel Ni-Co-W based superalloy was investigated using thermodynamic
calculations, scanning electron microscopy (SEM), electron probe microanalysis (EPMA), and
transmission electron microscopy (TEM). The results indicate that both the quantity and size of MC
carbides increase with higher C content, and numerous small M23C6 carbide precipitates form at grain
