alters the fracture behavior of the alloy, and effectively enhances its creep life. Additionally,
during creep, increased grain boundary strength allows more dislocations to be transferred at grain
boundaries, resulting in more stacking faults and microtwins forming at service temperature. These
stacking faults and microtwins hinder further dislocation movement, thereby achieving synergistic
strengthening of both the grain boundaries and the intragranular regions. As the temperature further
increases to 850 °C, the grain boundary strength diminishes, and the efficiency of C in
strengthening the grain boundaries decreases accordingly. Nonetheless, C can still effectively
strengthen the grain boundaries of the alloy and inhibit the formation of grain boundary cracks
during creep.

