creep and without substantial compositional changes. Borides at 850 °C were found to coarsen,
resulting in some cases into γ′- depleted zones, where, however, no cracks were observed. The major
consequences of secondary phases on the microstructural stability of superalloys during the design
of new polycrystalline superalloys are discussed.

