2026-01-26 22:30:31,780 [INFO] root - [5] 来源: Influence of powder particle size on the microstructure of a hot isostatically pressed superalloy (块: None)
The influence of powder particle size on the microstructure of the powder metallurgy superalloy
FGH97 was investigated. The powder atomized by the plasma rotating electrode process was sieved to
three types: fine powder (0C53μm), medium-sized powder (53C150μm), and coarse powder (150C212μm),
which were all characterized by their nearly perfect spherical shape and low oxygen content. The
powder was filled, degassed, sealed, and then densified by hot isostatic pressing. Then the
microstructures of the fully dense compacts were characterized. The results show that fine powder
led to limited plastic deformation of particles during densification, resulting in a minimum of 3
boundaries and modest PPB (Previous Particle Boundary) decoration. The fine powder compact showed
that low impact toughness was caused by fracture along the PPB. However, the addition of Nb and Hf
promoted the formation of the dispersed stable MC particles inside the grain, thus preventing the
diffusion of C to the surface of the powder particles to form M6C carbides, and resulting in little
tendency to present PPB for this alloy. Therefore, the medium-sized powder and coarse powder compact
did not present PPB. Thus, the medium-sized powder is optimal for HIP compact preparation, given
that fine powder produced PPB while the coarse powder increased the grain size.

2026-01-26 22:30:31,780 [INFO] root - [6] 来源: A new evaluation method of mixed-grain in finite element simulation during ring-rolling of superalloy (块: None)
A new evaluation method for mixed-grain structures caused by incomplete recrystallization during the
ring-rolling of superalloys has been established. This method can accurately predict the
microstructure uniformity of ring forgings, demonstrating good agreement with experimental results.
By applying the established method, the influence of initial grain size on the microstructure
uniformity of ring forgings was systematically analyzed. The results revealed that the initial grain
size condition can be assessed more rigorously, leading to significantly improved microstructure
uniformity in the final forging. Additionally, this evaluation method is not only applicable to the
analysis of initial grain size but can also be extended to investigate the effects of other process
parameters. Furthermore, it holds potential for broader applications in other hot deformation
processes, such as cogging or die forging.

2026-01-26 22:30:31,781 [INFO] root - [7] 来源: Effect of Nano-Sized α Phase on the Ultrasonic and Mechanical Properties of Ni-Based Superalloy (块: None)
The effect of the nano-sized α phase on the ultrasonic and mechanical properties of the IN939
superalloy was investigated. The results indicate that the microstructure characteristics of the
nano-sized α phase directly affected the ultrasonic longitudinal velocity, the attenuation
coefficient, and the mechanical properties. The ultrasonic longitudinal velocity increased with the
volume fraction of the α phase, whereas the attenuation coefficient was similar to the fractional
change in the  channel width. The lower fractional change in the  channel width, in combination with
a high volume fraction of the α phase, was conducive to improving the mechanical properties of the
superalloy. Additionally, the variation in the ultrasonic properties could reflect the variation in
the mechanical properties of the IN939 superalloy, which was beneficial for optimizing the heat
treatment process and characterizing the α phase precipitation behavior in a nondestructive manner.

2026-01-26 22:30:31,781 [INFO] root - [8] 来源: Mechanical properties and deformation mechanism at elevated temperatures of IN718 superalloy processed by powder forging (块: None)
A novel powder forging route was employed herein to consolidate the IN718 superalloy from prealloyed
powders. A near full-density, absence of prior particles boundaries (PPB) network, near-isotropic
properties were obtained in the proposed powder forged slab. A synergistic combination of strength
and ductility was achieved due to minimized prior particle boundaries and its broken network during
powder forging. Chemical homogeneity enhanced the uniform distribution of γʺ and γˊ precipitates in
the matrix, as well as leading to a very small fraction of metal carbides (MC) and oxides. Equiaxed
grains achieved in different forging directions led to near-isotropic mechanical properties in the
forged slab. These results indicate that powder forging can emerge as a promising technique for
consolidating powder metallurgy superalloys as an alternative technique to the conventional HIP, hot
extrusion and additive processing techniques. In the present investigation of stress-strain curves,
serrations were observed in the samples tested at 550 °C, 650 °C, 700 °C and 750 °C in as-forged and
heat treated conditions. According to the present study, the diffusion of interstitial C and
substitutional solute atoms like Nb and Mo is primarily responsible for the formation of
DSA/serrations at high temperatures in as-forged conditions. On the other hand, in heat-treated
conditions, interstitial C and substitutional Mo become more significant. Nb plays a significant
role in the occurrence of serration when it is in solid solution state instead of precipitate state.
Further, TEM micrographs of deformed specimens were also analysed to determine the deformation
mechanisms at elevated temperatures.

