2026-01-26 23:07:09,339 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 1 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'The δ-Ni₂Al₃ phase is expected to form at the outer surface of the coating when using a high activity aluminizing process. This is because high activity packs provide a higher chemical potential of aluminum, enabling rapid aluminum diffusion into the substrate and promoting the formation of aluminum-rich phases like δ-Ni₂Al₃ and hyperstoichiometric β-NiAl (>51 at% Al). Since aluminum is the main diffusing species in these phases, the coating grows inward as aluminum diffuses from the surface into the nickel-rich superalloy substrate, reacting to form intermetallic layers beneath the original surface. In contrast, low activity packs supply less aluminum, resulting in slower diffusion and lower Al availability at the surface. This can lead to incomplete reaction or poor densification of the coating layer, increasing the likelihood that unreacted pack particles become mechanically embedded in the porous or loosely adherent outer surface of the coating. [cite: chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-1, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-e-4, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-e-3, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-r-3, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-r-4, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-6, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-r-5]', 'score': 9}]
