The oxidation behavior of K38G superalloy, which is mechanically polished or sand blasted and then
coated with glass matrix composite coatings, is investigated at 1000°C. Results indicate that sand
blasting pre-treatment enhances the resistance to oxidation and spallation of the glass coatings on
superalloys by promoting formation of an alumina interlayer. The most important factors favoring
