vanadium hot corrosion at both low and high temperatures. During hot corrosion, the Co-modified
coating develops a multilayered oxide structure consisting of CoO/CoAl2O4/Al2O3. This unique
microstructure formation can be attributed to the synergistic effects of Co-induced suppression of
outward Al diffusion in the coating and the dissolution of the outer Al2O3 scale by VO3- ions.
