2026-01-26 23:19:03,663 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 14 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'Under severe hot corrosion conditions or at temperatures above 1050℃, NiCoCrAlY coatings are more appropriate than pack aluminised coatings due to their superior hot corrosion resistance. These coatings can be deposited using cold spray techniques. Additionally, Ni–20Cr and Stellite 6 alloys also exhibit hot corrosion resistance and are typically deposited via High-velocity oxy-fuel (HVOF). [cite: chunk-f3608000f08ffe8ebee2968f53c82d81-e-2, chunk-cc0a5dcc8fc2f75d2420dc4f27988ac7-e-2, chunk-56b0eb371d2d07d16875784eac6b361c-e-15, chunk-08b2efb9cb22c2ae928949867d82aad0-e-2, chunk-23267169f45c7f754fc1bdd63cb46b98-e-1, chunk-c44ae8e72689fc1052830e6d43e224ef-e-1, chunk-fc3e50625686cfbe77e9056b36f06b03-r-9, chunk-fc3e50625686cfbe77e9056b36f06b03-r-3, chunk-fc3e50625686cfbe77e9056b36f06b03-r-4, chunk-c44ae8e72689fc1052830e6d43e224ef-r-20, chunk-a594744f82c9617f0f80be71a70d4e19-r-1, chunk-c44ae8e72689fc1052830e6d43e224ef-r-12, chunk-7432b1609645013cfac5ae9f15146880-r-6, chunk-c44ae8e72689fc1052830e6d43e224ef-r-3]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'For applications involving severe hot corrosion or temperatures above 1050\u202f°C, Al–Cr compositional gradient coatings are more appropriate. These coatings are deposited using multi-arc ion plating technology (MIPT) onto Co–Al–W substrates, and they demonstrate enhanced high-temperature oxidation resistance—forming a protective three-layer oxidation structure when exposed to 1000\u202f°C for 20–60\u202fmin. Although tested just below 1050\u202f°C, their structural evolution and thermal stability suggest suitability for extreme conditions where pack aluminising fails [cite: chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-e-1, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-e-3, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-e-6, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-e-7, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-e-9, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-r-2, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-r-6, chunk-9a4a85b754d1e614643e1e2041bc1770-r-10]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Under severe hot corrosion conditions or at temperatures above 1050℃, modified aluminide coatings are more appropriate than standard pack aluminide coatings. These enhanced coatings can be directly applied onto nickel-base alloys—common substrates in high-temperature aerospace and industrial components—to provide improved resistance to oxidation, hot corrosion, and thermal fatigue [cite: chunk-fcbc303510123ec9a73946e08a77134f-e-10, chunk-fcbc303510123ec9a73946e08a77134f-e-9, chunk-fcbc303510123ec9a73946e08a77134f-r-7].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Under severe hot corrosion conditions or temperatures above 1050℃, α-Al₂O₃/NiAl multilayer coatings are more appropriate due to their enhanced performance over standard aluminide coatings. These advanced coatings can be deposited using methods such as pack cementation or reactive air aluminizing (RAA), with alloying strategies like rhodium incorporation into β-NiAl further improving high-temperature stability and oxidation resistance. [cite: chunk-9fcc4b5b57297f807d05e8927ccf2eed-e-4, chunk-dfe2f1887dc7e61661390cb2b77598da-e-11, chunk-9fcc4b5b57297f807d05e8927ccf2eed-r-10, chunk-6949730e3425ced498facd9487bde888-e-2, chunk-aedbe4412d2761c1e12ab362e44dea99-e-3, chunk-2e5bf8dae3f8176658fa11aedcbb87c2-e-1, chunk-5eb845f9b1000550792febcc31b14308-r-2, chunk-0e56d036a3d2e550af5ea66665ba607a-e-6, chunk-0e80afe39178e4dd865f53d647dccf91-e-1, chunk-0e80afe39178e4dd865f53d647dccf91-r-5]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Under severe hot corrosion conditions or at temperatures above 1050℃, plasma spray coatings and physical vapour deposition (PVD) coatings are more appropriate alternatives to pack aluminisation. Plasma spray coating processes—both current and future-oriented—were actively researched in 1986 as robust solutions for high-temperature environments, with studies authored by R. C. Tucker, B. J. Gill, and a team including A. R. Nicholl. Physical vapour deposition, as documented by D. H. Boone in the same context, is presented as a complementary advanced coating technology suitable for similar demanding applications. These methods are particularly relevant for protecting components made from or coated with MCrAlY alloys, which are critical in thermal barrier systems and evaluated for oxidation and high-temperature corrosion resistance. [cite: chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-e-13, chunk-fc5aa264fb28225ff63c38a7e3698291-e-7, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-e-7, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-e-8, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-e-6, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-e-5, chunk-fc5aa264fb28225ff63c38a7e3698291-r-4, chunk-fc5aa264fb28225ff63c38a7e3698291-r-5, chunk-fc5aa264fb28225ff63c38a7e3698291-r-6, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-4, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-5, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-6, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-7, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-8, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-9, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-10, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-11, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-12, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-13, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-14, chunk-28027332c1e907d2b9fb62cbdc68fd6c-r-15]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'NiCoCr-based superalloy coatings are more appropriate for severe conditions such as high-temperature or corrosive environments exceeding the limits of pack aluminisation (e.g., above 1050℃ or under severe hot corrosion). These coatings can be enhanced through N-doping to improve surface hardness, oxidation resistance, and wear performance, making them suitable for performance-critical applications like gas turbines or hypersonic vehicles. They are deposited using directed energy deposition (DED), an additive manufacturing technique that enables localized, high-precision application—ideal for repair or functional coating of high-value components in aerospace and energy sectors [cite: chunk-de6dfc442a87271c5105832db3fc4328-e-1, chunk-de6dfc442a87271c5105832db3fc4328-e-2, chunk-de6dfc442a87271c5105832db3fc4328-e-3, chunk-de6dfc442a87271c5105832db3fc4328-r-1, chunk-de6dfc442a87271c5105832db3fc4328-r-2].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Under severe hot corrosion conditions or at temperatures above 1050℃, platinum aluminide coatings are more appropriate than standard pack aluminide coatings. These enhanced coatings can be deposited using either high activity or low activity aluminizing processes, with the choice of method influencing oxidation resistance and microstructural development. Platinum concentration in the coating further enhances performance by improving oxidation resistance and stabilizing beneficial microstructures. [cite: chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-1, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-e-17, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-r-1, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-3, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-r-2, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-e-12, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-r-2, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-e-4, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-e-3, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-r-3, chunk-27d4439c082e1df0f703012a02b14ffb-r-4, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-6, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-r-5, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-e-16, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-e-15, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-e-14, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-r-10, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-r-11, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-e-17, chunk-b740c8122a3674caed65056e75488d1f-r-12, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-4, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-r-4, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-e-5, chunk-23667ab4826d0039e851f5cb53aa5455-r-3]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'For severe hot corrosion conditions or temperatures above 1050℃, ZrB2/HfB2-doped and MoSi2–MoB coatings are more appropriate alternatives. Both coating systems can be deposited via pulsed electrospark deposition (PED) onto the nickel-based superalloy EP741NP, which is used in aerospace applications. The ZrB2/HfB2-doped variant shows broader integration with high-temperature intermetallic phases (e.g., β-MoSi2, γ-phase, Mo5Si3) and stronger adhesion to EP741NP, suggesting enhanced performance under extreme conditions compared to the undoped MoSi2–MoB coating. [cite: chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-11, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-10, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-13, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-4, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-4, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-3, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-6, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-5, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-9, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-8, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-7, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-e-6, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-8, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-16, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-10, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-12, chunk-c8d2204467b10fe5246ebc6260841c9b-r-14]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Pt-modified coatings are more appropriate for severe high-temperature conditions above 1050°C, as they demonstrate improved resistance to cyclic oxidation at 1150°C despite some performance suppression from voids beneath the oxide scale [cite: chunk-c4c7b0affa01848bc8e4f191e15bca11-e-10, chunk-c4c7b0affa01848bc8e4f191e15bca11-e-9, chunk-c4c7b0affa01848bc8e4f191e15bca11-r-8, chunk-c4c7b0affa01848bc8e4f191e15bca11-e-7, chunk-c4c7b0affa01848bc8e4f191e15bca11-r-9].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Under severe hot corrosion conditions or temperatures above 1050℃, Re-Hf co-doped β-NiAl coatings and (Ni,Pt)Al coatings are more appropriate. These advanced coatings interact with TCP-associated interdiffusion zones (IDZ) and can be deposited using Arc Ion Plating (AIP). Specifically, Re-Hf co-doped β-NiAl is prepared via AIP and resides within the IDZ, while TCP phases promote the precipitation of refurbished (Ni,Pt)Al coatings, offering enhanced high-temperature performance compared to conventional pack aluminide coatings. [cite: chunk-2ff810fcd7689b33f6f72b9eeab502ca-r-4, chunk-2ff810fcd7689b33f6f72b9eeab502ca-r-2, chunk-aec0dfc5a9ab34c0be79fbc4f9679c5f-r-4]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Under severe conditions such as hot corrosion or temperatures above 1050℃, EB-PVD YSZ (electron beam–physical vapor deposition yttria-stabilized zirconia) coatings are more appropriate than alternatives like plasma-sprayed YSZ. EB-PVD YSZ coatings demonstrate significantly higher durability, as evidenced by increased cycles to failure compared to plasma-sprayed variants. This performance advantage is attributed to the columnar microstructure of EB-PVD coatings, which provides better strain tolerance and thermal cycling resistance. The Rene N5/Pt-Al/EB-PVD YSZ system, in particular, shows consistent spallation life, making it a reliable choice for high-temperature applications. [cite: chunk-60aaf9203ef3ac8be9f25ac9c0695fd4-e-5, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-e-7, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-r-2, chunk-60aaf9203ef3ac8be9f25ac9c0695fd4-e-5, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-e-8, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-r-3, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-e-1, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-e-10, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-r-4, chunk-60aaf9203ef3ac8be9f25ac9c0695fd4-e-5, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-e-1, chunk-a9c0bc9f9a3da960898d5e1e2fbfd012-r-1]', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'For severe hot corrosion conditions or temperatures above 1050\u202f°C, thermal/environmental barrier coatings (TEBCs) with multi-layered architectures are more appropriate than pack aluminide coatings. The TEBC system described includes a CoNiCrAlY bond coat, a Y2O3-stabilized ZrO2 thermal insulation layer, and a ceramic top layer composed of mullite (Al6Si2O13) and hexacelsian (BaAl2Si2O8), which collectively enhance high-temperature durability and environmental resistance. While the context does not explicitly state the deposition method, such advanced TEBC systems are typically applied via techniques like electron beam–physical vapor deposition (EB-PVD) or air plasma spraying (APS), consistent with turbine blade coating practices. [cite: chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-e-1, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-e-2, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-e-3, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-e-4, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-e-5, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-e-8, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-r-1, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-r-2, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-r-3, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-r-4, chunk-f48bc93894ffd7a45917cb089a79065b-r-7]', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'For severe hot corrosion conditions or temperatures above 1050℃, plasma-sprayed yttria-stabilized zirconia (YSZ) top coats applied over MCrAlY bond coats on superalloy substrates (e.g., MarM509) are more appropriate. These thermal barrier coating (TBC) systems provide enhanced high-temperature protection compared to pack aluminide coatings. The YSZ layer is deposited via plasma spraying, while the underlying MCrAlY bond coat is typically applied using methods like vacuum plasma spraying or electron beam physical vapor deposition. [cite: E1]', 'score': 8}, {'answer': 'The inorganic salt aluminum coating TWL12+TWL20 is applied to Ni-based powder metallurgy (P/M) superalloys and shows potential for protecting aeroengine P/M superalloys, suggesting it may be suitable under severe conditions such as high-temperature or hot corrosion environments where conventional pack aluminising coatings offer limited protection. The coating is deposited via an inorganic salt-based process rather than traditional pack cementation [cite: chunk-92765e59dc9cfd1e503d787c28a8645b-e-1, chunk-92765e59dc9cfd1e503d787c28a8645b-e-2, chunk-92765e59dc9cfd1e503d787c28a8645b-r-1, chunk-92765e59dc9cfd1e503d787c28a8645b-e-10, chunk-92765e59dc9cfd1e503d787c28a8645b-r-12]', 'score': 7}]
