2026-01-26 23:31:08,171 [INFO] root - [14] 来源: Effect of Pt on the microstructure and oxidation behavior of NiCrAlYSi+AlY coating on a Ni-based superalloy (块: None)
The NiCrAlYSi+Al, NiCrAlYSi+AlY and Pt modified NiCrAlYSi+AlY coatings were produced by combining
arc ion plating, electroplating Pt and annealing treatment. Isothermal oxidation and cyclic
oxidation behaviors of all coatings were investigated. The Pt modified NiCrAlYSi+AlY coating showed
the best oxidation resistance because the Pt addition decreased the oxidation rate and Al
consumption in the coating. The “oxide pegs” were observed at the interface between oxide scale and
Pt modified NiCrAlYSi+AlY coating after cyclic oxidation. The formation mechanism of coating and the
effects of Pt and Y addition on the oxidation performance of coating were discussed.

2026-01-26 23:31:08,171 [INFO] root - [15] 来源: The influence of high temperature on DV-2 jet engine Ni-based superalloy turbine blade degradation (块: None)
Blades and vanes made from Ni – and Co – base superalloys that are used in the hot section of all
gas turbine engines are coated to enhance resistance to hot corrosion. The most widely used coatings
are those based on the intermetallic compounds NiAl and CoAl, which are formed by diffusion
interaction of aluminium with surfaces of the nickel and cobalt alloys, respectively. Simple
aluminide coatings resist high – temperature oxidation by the formation of protective layer of
alumina and can be used up to about 1,150°C. The coatings degrade by loss of aluminium due to
spalling of oxides under thermal cycling conditions. HPT blades of DV – 2 jet engines are made from
Ni – based superalloy ŽS6K. For improving alloy’s high temperature resistance are blades coated with
Al – Si diffusion layer. Depending on jet engine flying regime an overcrossing of working
temperature may occur. It may result into coarsening of the gamma prime particles, thus decreasing
its strengthening effect. A real case study of DV-2 jet engine turbine blades after high temperature
exposition is discussed in this article.

2026-01-26 23:31:08,172 [INFO] root - [16] 来源: Low inter-diffusivity γ'-base bondcoats for single crystal superalloy René N5. Ⅱ: Cyclic oxidation behavior at 1100 ºC (块: None)
Three γ'-base coatings of Hf-doped and Re-modified NiCoCrAlTaY system were deposited on René N5
superalloy by magnetron sputtering. The cyclic oxidation behavior of these coatings was investigated
at 1100 °C for 500 h. The γ'-base coatings exhibited excellent resistance against coating/substrate
interdiffusion and coating rumpling. The TGO was mainly alumina. Minor TGO spallation occurred on
coatings with ˜19 at.% and 20 at.% Al, which may be correlated with the formation of Ta-rich oxide
particles within TGO scales, while severe TGO spallation occurred on coating with ˜25 at.% Al, which
may be correlated with the formation of voids at TGO/coating interface.

2026-01-26 23:31:08,172 [INFO] root - [17] 来源: Oxidation behaviour of Pt modified aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating on a Ni-based single crystal superalloy (块: None)
An aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating and Pt modified aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating were prepared on a Ni-
based superalloy. Isothermal and cyclic oxidation behaviour of both coatings were investigated. The
Pt modified aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating showed an enhanced oxidation resistance due to the presence
of Pt decreasing the oxidation rate and improving the adherence of alumina scale. The addition of Pt
in aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating inhibited the phase transformation from β to γ′. Besides, the
surface rumpling of Pt modified aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating was suppressed as compared to the
aluminized NiCrAlYSi coating.

