adherence, and prevent outward diffusion of refractory elements (such as W and Mo) from the
substrate. Overall, the presence of yttrium, tantalum, and silicon in the coating improved the
resistance of high temperature oxidation and enhanced the bonding force of the coating and the
alloy.

