A Ni+CrAlYSiN composite coating was prepared on a Ni-based superalloy K417 by vacuum arc
evaporation, mainly consists of nanocrystalline γ-Ni, fcc-AlN and fcc-CrN. The oxidation behaviour
of the specimens in air at 1000°C for 100h was studied. A double-layer oxide scale, inner Al2O3
layer and outer mixture layer mainly dominated by NiCr2O4, formed on the composite coating.
