2026-01-26 23:45:52,306 [INFO] root - Reduce阶段：筛选出 3 个高质量关键点，内容如下：[{'answer': 'Recent findings suggest that the ratcheting mechanism emphasized in early work by Evans and co-workers may not be truly operative, as microstructural models of damage evolution—accounting for diffusional reactions at and beneath the thermally grown oxide (TGO)—can inherently capture or even eliminate the need for invoking macroscopic ratcheting behavior. This implies that early reliance on ratcheting may have overlooked dominant microscale mechanisms like grain boundary diffusion and void nucleation [cite: chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-3, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-4, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-r-2].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'Given that microstructural modeling negates the necessity of the ratcheting mechanism and that ratcheting itself derives from macroscopic mechanical principles, a paradigm shift toward high-fidelity microstructural simulations is supported. This questions the continued relevance of ratcheting-centric models for TBC failure, especially in light of later observations emphasizing diffusional reactions [cite: chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-3, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-4, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-5, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-r-2, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-r-3].', 'score': 9}, {'answer': 'While the ratcheting mechanism is theoretically grounded in classical mechanics, its applicability to thermal barrier coating failure may be limited when microstructural damage processes—such as those occurring at the TGO interface—are dominant. This challenges the foundational assumptions of the late 1990s models and suggests they may lack fidelity in capturing true failure physics [cite: chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-4, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-e-5, chunk-db78ddbf62abad0b3c908872d469b5fa-r-3].', 'score': 8}]
